+# Create4: bounded existing-CLI operation host (review only)
+
+No checkout file was changed and no adapter/worker/device was run. Assets15 and Snapshot5 remain frozen. This is a proposed prerequisite, not full Create source admission.
+
+## Actual path and incompatibility
+
+* catalog.json feature-create executes modules/feature_journey.py --area create (1560s module deadline, existing full-capability requirements).
+* Module constructs OverteSession; Journey invokes session.feature_operation -> session._invoke -> module_support.operation -> adapter_client.invoke. process_identity/assert_process/assert_foreground also use module_support.operation.
+* adapter_client.invoke resolves manifest.command and runs a NEW subprocess per operation. It strips exactly six policy/reader/control keys and uses60s normally,120s for permission.snapshot/permission.set/snapshot.files,240s for app.install/app.upgrade.
+* The actual bound path is tests/device/adapters/android/adapter.py -> cli/attach_binding -> fixed pico4/binding.py -> create_adapter once PER PROCESS. The unrelated android/vr/pico/device-tests/adapter.py legacy adapter is not the selected implementation seam.
+* Pico _candidate_arguments snapshots exact vars(args) types/values, all environment, cwd and verifier identities. CandidateReadSeal pins original candidate inputs. Updating args.operation/args.arguments/action/target per request would poison this original admission.
+* _create_journey currently constructs PicoCreateJourney each call. Retaining only AndroidAdapter is insufficient: the actual Parent object, source lock, readers, original child program/FD owners and waitpid ownership must remain warm as well.
+* Parent.issue_peer_scope binds actual host PID/start/boot. peer_input_boundary requires the original live LinuxChatObserverProcess and holds original Parent lock plus worker source lock. Parent.accept_peer_return itself obtains actual waitpid(pid,WNOHANG)==(pid,0); an unrelated coordinator must not reap that worker first.
+* Journey.execute calls activate BEFORE continuity/act, including cleanup activation. A host transport by itself does not serialize that activation with Actor acquisition.
+
+## Proposed first reviewable packet: transport prerequisite only
+
+1. Add explicit Pico/native-binding operation-host mode to the EXISTING Android CLI. Parse one immutable Namespace and construct exactly the normal bound adapter once. Each request keeps local operation/arguments values, validates their existing contract, and calls that SAME adapter.invoke. No request mutates Namespace, cwd or env, imports another adapter, selects another target or discovers one.
+2. Add an explicit OverteSession operation context using a context-local adapter_client owner. Existing module_support.operation and helper calls automatically reuse the scoped transport because they already call invoke. Outside that context invoke retains its exact existing subprocess.run path; Phone/iOS/default behavior stays unchanged. Reject a changed manifest/target/nested foreign context instead of spawning another process. No global daemon or socket.
+3. One Popen child per journey, stdio only, sequential strict JSON request IDs and bounded frames/stderr. First operation's original60/120/240 timer starts before manifest pin/spawn/factory/dispatch; every later timer starts before send/checks. Factory, dispatch, complete response, physical/program rechecks and copy consume that SAME deadline. A phase-boundary bracket will later share its act deadline instead of adding independent begin+act budgets. The existing module deadline is still the total lifetime bound.
+4. Pin canonical manifest original bytes/hash/physical/OFD and actual resolved Python executable/entrypoint and source-owned prefix. Permit the opt-in only for the reviewed Android --kind pico --native-binding route with explicit target. Reuse OriginalDescriptor and original scope/file guards; do not misuse LinuxChatObserverProcess's exact --config grammar as generic operation-host admission. A small exact-cmdline owner can reuse its actual /proc PID/start/boot/exe/OFD predicates without changing the observer class. Child checks actual direct parent identity at startup, request boundaries and bounded idle waits.
+5. Snapshot and strip the EXISTING six env keys before Popen, then keep env/cwd immutable. Never serialize image policy, reader/control credentials, expectedFacts or requested verdicts. Strict operation validators remain the argument boundary; transport metadata is only version/id/operation/arguments/deadline. Reject duplicate keys, malformed IDs, unexpected replies, output overflow, changed files/program/parent, EOF and timeout. Record pending original request before delivery. Any uncertain write/read/result permanently poisons that owner: no replay/new host/fallback and no successful cleanup receipt. Preserve available raw originals. Actual owned child wait/exit and absence are host transport facts only, never app/Qt/native resource cleanup.
+6. Closing stdio never calls adapter.cleanup or sends product input. Successful host exit requires original process identity, actual kernel status, original FD checks and no unresolved host request/boundary/owned worker. Failure termination/reaping, if necessary, is restricted to the exact owned process and leaves application/worker/resource ownership unresolved. It cannot create a second Parent to repair the failed run.
+
+Proposed runtime files for packet A: adapter_client.py; overte_session.py; adapters/android/adapter.py (Pico-only mode); new adapters/pico4/operation_host.py (server/protocol); new adapter_operation_host.py (client/process/file ownership). No binding.py change in this packet. Explicit session context exists but no catalog/journey capability is promoted.
+
+Tests: device-free actual Popen fake of the same CLI construction seam, successive operations showing one adapter/host, exact original parent identity/zero kernel exit, first factory cost included in deadline, all6 keys absent, policy/expectedFacts refusal, args/env/cwd byte/type stability, real parent loss, changed/same-byte-replaced manifest/entry, actual same-inode recycled FD, stdout/stderr/partial JSON/duplicate ID/timeout/unknown delivery, no second spawn/replay, no automatic app cleanup. Assert every existing default subprocess deadline and Phone/iOS path unchanged. No compiler or device invocation.
+
+## Required subsequent Create composition before ordinary module enablement
+
+Retain the actual factory-created PicoCreateJourney once per fixed target/run inside that same operation host, not merely its serialized header. The Parent owns issue_peer_scope, actual feature_observer.py child launch/config and LinuxChatObserverProcess, nonce acceptance, zero-exit waitpid, final independent quiet and archive responsibilities. Reuse the current reviewed production worker and Parent methods unchanged; the module must not become their OS parent or reap their child.
+
+Add a DEFAULT-NOOP optional input context to existing Journey, supplied by the opt-in session, wrapping ticket publication through the normal act/cleanup call and its original return checks. It must cover baseline, ordinary steps, special retries and cleanup activation. With an active issued peer this context enters the ACTUAL Parent.peer_input_boundary BEFORE client.activate and holds that exact original worker owner/lock until ordinary input returns. Before a worker exists, any Parent-only locking is explicitly weaker and cannot claim peer serialization. Enter/exit fail closed and carry one original operation deadline; uncertain begin/activation/act/end is never replayed. If runner dies while a boundary is held, bounded parent/pipe checks fail the host and retain ownership. No fake cancellation or renewed worker deadline.
+
+This requires narrowly reviewed edits to modules/feature_journey.py, feature_journeys/engine.py and the private Pico coordinator/binding factory. It does not move policy/provider control into the child: existing client.activate remains in the common module between enter and act. Full feature.create.* remains closed until actual normal Parent factory, independent effect sources/Actor, before-activate boundary and final original retirement compose. The transport prerequisite alone cannot truthfully advertise them.
+
+## Main review risks
+
+* A context limited to session._invoke would miss process/foreground/probe helpers; use the existing adapter_client context boundary.
+* A stdio server that catches a write/CAS failure and continues can repeat real input. Uncertainty is permanent for that owner.
+* A generic per-request mutation of parsed args invalidates CandidateReadSeal; keep its admitted Namespace untouched.
+* A begin ACK does not release the actual lock. The same host thread must retain the real context until end or a bounded failure; do not substitute a JSON lock token.
+* Original worker waitpid belongs to the actual warm Parent. Host shutdown/transport zero exit does not retire its product graph.
+* Manifest resolution/bytes and executable ownership must be pinned, not just reloaded by pathname. Same-byte inode/OFD replacement is still foreign.
+* Exact request/frame-count and stdio size limits must be billed against current operation DTOs before implementation, with no existing deadline/cap raised. Stderr must drain boundedly to avoid pipe backpressure.
